From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Uzi Sarel <uzi.sarel@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Apr 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: max9296: add i2c write retry logic

The MAX9296 deserializer sits behind a PCA9548 I2C mux on Jetson Orin
platforms. Intermittent I2C write failures to the CTRL0 register (0x10)
during GMSL link setup cause the SERDES initialization to leave the
link in a partially-configured state.

Add retry logic to max9296_write_reg so that transient I2C failures
are handled transparently. Retry up to 3 times with 10ms delay between
attempts.

---
 drivers/media/i2c/max9296.c | 18 +++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/max9296.c b/drivers/media/i2c/max9296.c
index 92b483b6..a1b2c3d4 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/max9296.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/max9296.c
@@ -59,13 +59,21 @@ static int max9296_write_reg(struct device *dev,
 {
 	struct max9296 *priv = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	int err;
+	int retry;

-	err = regmap_write(priv->regmap, addr, val);
-	if (err)
-		dev_err(dev, "%s:i2c write failed, 0x%x = %x\n",
-			__func__, addr, val);
+	for (retry = 0; retry < 3; retry++) {
+		err = regmap_write(priv->regmap, addr, val);
+		if (!err)
+			return 0;
+		if (retry < 2) {
+			dev_warn(dev, "%s:i2c write failed (0x%x = 0x%x, err %d), retry %d\n",
+				 __func__, addr, val, err, retry + 1);
+			usleep_range(10000, 11000);
+		}
+	}

-	/* delay before next i2c command as required for SERDES link */
+	dev_err(dev, "%s:i2c write failed after 3 retries, 0x%x = 0x%x, err %d\n",
+		__func__, addr, val, err);
 	usleep_range(100, 110);

 	return err;
--
2.43.0

